- Waitlist — `/waitlist` + `POST /api/waitlist` implement the referral-loop pre-launch pattern: each signup gets a share code, referrals jump the queue (`lib/waitlist.ts`). Embed `components/waitlist-form.tsx` in the marketing page when launching pre-product. Position ranks by referrals then join order; never fake the counts. A join never reveals whether the address was already listed (CP §6.1): every join gets the same response and a fresh opaque viewer cookie, only a real insert stores it, so only the browser that joined sees its position and share link, via `GET /api/waitlist`. Keep it that way: add no lookup by email or share code. Joining is one atomic upsert, credits a referral only on a real insert, and sits behind an origin check and a per-IP limit (CP §6.3). Referral counts are not verified: someone with many IP addresses can still inflate one, so confirm new addresses by email before a count earns a real reward.
